{
 "question": "With the dither the same, Dolby's decode of an E-AC-3 stream has something in every coupled coefficient that its decode of the same source as AC-3 has not and that neither this decoder nor FFmpeg's makes (evidence 51). What is it, what sets it off, and can it be read?",
 "method": "Dolby's decoders were run as they stand and only what they write was read: the element of the Reference Player (`gst-launch-1.0 filesrc ! dlbac3parse ! dlbac3dec out-ch-config=<0, 7 or 11> drc-suppress=true drc-mode=custom-0 drc-cut=0 drc-boost=0 drop-delay=true ! audio/x-raw,format=F32LE ! filesink`) and the decode filter of the Dolby Encoding Engine (`ddp_decode`, 24-bit WAVE; `docs/dolby-tools.md`). Fifteen stereo test signals of twelve seconds, one thing apart from the next (`tools/coupling_mix.py signals`), were encoded by FFmpeg at 128 kbit/s as E-AC-3 and as AC-3; both encodes couple from coefficient 49 (4,6 kHz) in eight sub-bands and make the same exponents and coordinates. Each stream was decoded by Dolby's decoder and by this one with its dither on (the dither is Dolby's, evidence 51), both decodes were taken back to coefficients (windowed overlap-add is an orthogonal transform), and the two were set against each other in the channels' own region and in the coupled region (`tools/coupling_mix.py regions`). Where the coupled region stood apart, Dolby's coefficients were fitted on this decoder's coefficients of the same place in the block and in the blocks before, first with one weight for all blocks, then by turns the weights of every block and sub-band with the filter held and the filter with the weights held, and the filter was read as an all-pass (`tools/coupling_mix.py mix`). Whether the filter runs before or after the coupling coordinate was asked of a stream whose coordinates move, with the coordinates this decoder read. A stream of a library is a number; the films are not in the repository.",
 "commands": [
  "python tools/coupling_mix.py signals <directory>",
  "ffmpeg -i <signal>.wav -c:a eac3 -b:a 128k -f eac3 <signal>-128-eac3.ec3   (and -c:a ac3 -f ac3)",
  "gst-launch-1.0 filesrc location=<stream> ! dlbac3parse ! dlbac3dec out-ch-config=0 drc-suppress=true drc-mode=custom-0 drc-cut=0 drc-boost=0 drop-delay=true ! audio/x-raw,format=F32LE ! filesink location=<reference>.f32",
  "dee --xml <job made of xml_templates/ddp_decode/ec3_ddp_decode_wav_manifest.xml>",
  "oadec decode <stream> -o <ours>.wav",
  "oadec eac3-blocks --frame 100 <stream>   (cplbegf 1, cplendf 6: the first coupled coefficient 49, eight sub-bands)",
  "python tools/coupling_mix.py regions <reference>.f32 <ours>.wav --channels 2 --first 49 --sub-bands 8",
  "python tools/coupling_mix.py mix <reference>.f32 <ours>.wav --channels 2 --first 49 --sub-bands 8 --out <mix>.json",
  "python tools/coupling_mix.py mix <reference>.f32 <ours>.wav --channels 8 --first 97 --sub-bands 7 --learn 4",
  "gst-launch-1.0 filesrc ! dlbac3parse enable-metadata=true ! dlbac3dec out-ch-config=21 ... ! \"audio/x-raw(meta:DlbObjectAudioMeta),format=F32LE\" ! filesink   (the objects)",
  "python tools/joc_bands.py <ours>.atmos.audio <objects>.f32",
  "python tools/coupling_mix.py --self-check"
 ],
