  "public_documents": "US 9,489,956 (Audio signal enhancement using estimated spatial parameters) and US 9,830,916 (Signal decorrelation in an audio processing system), both of Dolby, describe a decoder that decorrelates the coupled channels of an AC-3 or E-AC-3 stream with an all-pass along the blocks after a fixed delay and a weight estimated from the bands under the coupling begin frequency, with noise added to it. What was measured has that shape. Nothing was taken from them into the decoder.",
